{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Part of this video was sponsored by\nLastPass. Stick around to the end for a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3600,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "word from our sponsor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5200,
    "dDurationMs": 2702,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Are negative ions\ngood for you?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7902,
    "dDurationMs": 2236,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Normally I'd dismiss such a question out of hand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10138,
    "dDurationMs": 2432,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact that's\nexactly what I did when a friend brought"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12570,
    "dDurationMs": 3239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it up about a month ago. But he was\ninsistent he said no this is for real"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15809,
    "dDurationMs": 1191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's science behind it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17000,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so I\nlooked into it and I found this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21000,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are literally hundreds of published\npeer-reviewed scientific studies on the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25560,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "biological effects of ions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28220,
    "dDurationMs": 1629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a body\nof research that begins about a century"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29849,
    "dDurationMs": 3211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ago and continues to the present day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33060,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And\nthis is just a fraction of it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35220,
    "dDurationMs": 5159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now these studies aren't just about any old ions\nthey're about atmospheric ions or air"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40379,
    "dDurationMs": 4921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ions. And although the results are not\nuniform, they all begin with the premise"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45300,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that positive ions make us feel bad and\nnegative ions make us feel good."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50260,
    "dDurationMs": 5780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in this video I want to get to the bottom\nof this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59000,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are Himalayan salt lamps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60960,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With the heat from the light bulb, it\nreleases negative ions into the air and of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64650,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "course negative ions are what you\nbreathe in and produce the serotonin in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68760,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the body and in serotonin is like the\nprimary neurotransmitter in your whole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75360,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "body and all living things and that's\nwhat makes you feel good..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78840,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "awesome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81000,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can I jump in here for a second.\nWhen I first heard all this business"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84780,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about atmospheric ions, my first thought\nwas 'why should we expect there to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88860,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many ions in the atmosphere at all?' I\nmean to recap, an ion is just an atom or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93900,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a molecule that has gained or lost an\nelectron. If it loses an electron it's a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99060,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "positive ion. If it gains an electron it\nbecomes a negative ion. But here's the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103590,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thing: unlike charges attract.\nSo moving about in the atmosphere I'd"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107820,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "expect the positive and negative ions to\nfind each other and then BOOM they're"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111540,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back to being neutral."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114000,
    "dDurationMs": 4049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, as it\nturns out there are some processes that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118049,
    "dDurationMs": 3251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are constantly generating atmospheric\nions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121300,
    "dDurationMs": 2209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example cosmic rays. These are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123509,
    "dDurationMs": 4651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "highly energetic particles from across\nthe universe that slam into our"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128160,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "atmosphere and transfer their energy to\nthe air, creating ions in the process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132540,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Cosmic rays are thought to\ncreate around 500 ions per cubic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137430,
    "dDurationMs": 3839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "centimeter at ground level. In fact\nthey're the most significant source of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141269,
    "dDurationMs": 2731,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ions generated over the oceans."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144000,
    "dDurationMs": 3359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But here\non land there are other sources of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147359,
    "dDurationMs": 4861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ionization, things like natural\nradioactivity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152220,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are these long-lived"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153540,
    "dDurationMs": 5130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isotopes of uranium and thorium and\ntheir decay products that can spit out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158670,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "highly energetic particles in the form\nof alpha, beta and gamma rays."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162600,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These ionize the air and they vary widely from\nplace to place but they can contribute"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169200,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hundreds up to many thousands of ions\nper cubic centimeter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176500,
    "dDurationMs": 5359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you were to recommend one of these to me that like\nhas the most negative ions, er, which one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181859,
    "dDurationMs": 781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "do you think?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182640,
    "dDurationMs": 1554,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would just go for which\none's hottest. -yeah?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184194,
    "dDurationMs": 4966,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because it's the heat from the lightbulb that creates the heat, which makes the reaction in the salt."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189160,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Got it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192000,
    "dDurationMs": 4939,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wow! This one's great.\nYeah? This would just be perfect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199500,
    "dDurationMs": 5909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then you have thunderstorms. Each\nlightning strike generates copious"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205409,
    "dDurationMs": 1411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "amounts of ions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208000,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Perhaps one of the more\nsurprising sources of negative ions is waterfalls."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212640,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As water droplets collide\nwith each other or with wetted surfaces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217110,
    "dDurationMs": 5519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with high velocity, the water molecules\ncreate this electrified spray with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222629,
    "dDurationMs": 3704,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "negative ions that can be transferred to\nthe air around it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226333,
    "dDurationMs": 6317,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Depending on your distance from the waterfall, ion levels\ncan reach tens of thousands of ions per"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232650,
    "dDurationMs": 6020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cubic centimeter. And the same effect\noccurs with ocean waves crashing on shore."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246500,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hello! \nHi Derek, how are you?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249340,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Good, Can I give you that? \nSure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251180,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what I want to know is how many negative ions are there coming off\nthat lamp when it's on?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257180,
    "dDurationMs": 7630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have a technique involving mass spectrometry\nthat measures negative ions coming off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264810,
    "dDurationMs": 3430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of solids and so we can give it a try."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268240,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Are you an ion expert? \nI've been studying"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271820,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ions for 55 years. \nWhoa"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276720,
    "dDurationMs": 1919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And have\nwritten hundreds of papers on all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278639,
    "dDurationMs": 3921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aspects of ions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282560,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is my salt lamp.\nit's meant to give us lots of negative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284520,
    "dDurationMs": 3419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ions. Can you tell me whether it's giving\nus some negative ions?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287939,
    "dDurationMs": 6361,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're gonna have a look and the thing we're utilizing here\nis that the inlet to this mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294300,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spectrometer is at atmospheric pressure\nand if there's ions there we'll be able"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297780,
    "dDurationMs": 5310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to detect them. So this is like.. is it is\nit kind of like an electronic nose or"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303090,
    "dDurationMs": 5850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something for ions? sniffs\nthe ions. - You could think of it as a nose for ions. Yeah, yeah, sniffs the ions. -OK"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308940,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The lamp is next to the ion sampling\ncone. I mean it's not on yet but we'll see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313350,
    "dDurationMs": 4289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if there's any ions coming from it. -No\nso this display here this would be this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317639,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is our mass to charge axis here so how\nhow heavy they are in molecular"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 322139,
    "dDurationMs": 4381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "weight essentially and if there's ions\nbeing formed we're gonna see some signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326520,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on this screen. -There'd be like some peaks? Some peaks, yeah"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330500,
    "dDurationMs": 1510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now does it need to warm up?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332010,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "er -I think that's the idea, yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 334860,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now\nthere are some places that do naturally"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338610,
    "dDurationMs": 5809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have lower concentrations of ions, namely\nthe interiors of houses and businesses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344419,
    "dDurationMs": 4601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because these structures provide some\nshielding from the cosmic rays and from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349020,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the natural radioactivity. Plus if you\nhave metal ducting and air"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354000,
    "dDurationMs": 4349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "conditioning, well some of those charged\nions will get stuck in the ducts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358349,
    "dDurationMs": 5130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so typically levels inside homes and\nbusinesses can be as low as around 100"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363479,
    "dDurationMs": 3521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or 200 ions per cubic centimeter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368000,
    "dDurationMs": 2889,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ion\nconcentrations are also typically lower"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370889,
    "dDurationMs": 5340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in polluted areas, in big cities or\naround factories. And that's because the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376229,
    "dDurationMs": 4741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ions actually cling to those\npollutants or the aerosols and so they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380970,
    "dDurationMs": 2090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "don't live as long in the atmosphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383060,
    "dDurationMs": 2470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So\nthe assertion that we live in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385530,
    "dDurationMs": 3746,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "environments with fewer ions than our\nancestors is true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389276,
    "dDurationMs": 5314,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you're thinking that you feel better\naround waterfalls and oceans and after"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394590,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thunderstorms than you do in polluted\ncities or around big factories, well"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398850,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "maybe that's the reason why scientists\nhave been studying the effects of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402840,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "negative ions on human health for nearly\na century."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407880,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's consider the evidence..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409710,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In one study people suffering from\nseasonal affective disorder were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414000,
    "dDurationMs": 3630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "randomly assigned to one of three\ntreatment groups: bright light therapy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417630,
    "dDurationMs": 4970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "high concentrations of negative ions or\nlow concentrations of negative ions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422600,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They found that both bright light therapy and high-density negative ions independently"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427050,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "produced antidepressant effects, but not\nlow density negative ions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431280,
    "dDurationMs": 6030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In another study, participants in a high-density negative\nion environment had significantly faster"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437310,
    "dDurationMs": 5690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reaction times and reported being more\nenergetic than those in an ambient air control."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443000,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if all this sounds too\nsubjective, EEG experiments showed people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447060,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exposed to high-density negative ions\nhad a slower alpha wave frequency with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451860,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "higher amplitude. Participants also\nreported increased relaxation, alertness,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 456510,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and improved working capacity. And\nopposite results have been found with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461010,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "positive ions. In one study volunteers\nwere exposed to high concentrations of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464970,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "positive ions for two hours. Symptoms of\nanxiety and excitement significantly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470010,
    "dDurationMs": 5190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "increased. During the time of exposure\nserum serotonin levels also increased"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 475200,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "significantly. This has even been taken\ninto real-world work environments. An"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479850,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "air ionizer was fitted to the\nair-conditioning unit in an office"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483300,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "building and periodically turned on and\noff over 12 weeks. When the ionizer was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487890,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pumping out negative ions, workers\nreported 50% fewer headaches. They also"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492480,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reported increased alertness, perceived\natmospheric freshness, and environmental"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497580,
    "dDurationMs": 4980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and personal warmth. It's feeling it's\nfeeling pretty hot it's been on for an"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502560,
    "dDurationMs": 6270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hour? yeah. So the question is can a salt\nlamp generate negative ions? let's check"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508830,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for negative ions?\n-let's look again"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514100,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Doesn't look like it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515600,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, I mean there's not even like a\nbackground."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524000,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, there's not... it's just like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527280,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's not even sitting there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531100,
    "dDurationMs": 3830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So your conclusion after testing this device is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534930,
    "dDurationMs": 5270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it's producing no negative ions.\n-We're certainly not able to detect any negative ions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540200,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The idea for how these\nsalt lamps are meant to create negative"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544080,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ions is that water molecules are meant\nto land on the surface and liberate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548760,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chloride ions from the lattice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551100,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But ask any chemist worth their salt and they'll"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554220,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tell you the energy required to do this\nis way too high so it just doesn't"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558660,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "happen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560340,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What I find ironic is that there\nare crystals which when heated will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564180,
    "dDurationMs": 3570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "produce ions.\nIt's just that salt doesn't have the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567750,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right crystal structure to make this\nwork. The gemstone tourmaline does."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571700,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those samples are worth many thousands of\ndollars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575140,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tourmaline has a structure such that if you heat it and cause it to expand, it will actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581580,
    "dDurationMs": 4710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "develop an electric charge on the faces\nof the of the crystal you have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 586290,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "discharges between those faces, breakdown in air and forming ions and that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590910,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "charge then can get transferred to any\norganic molecule that's present in the air."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595650,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A five degree change was enough to generate ions. \n-I just find this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599910,
    "dDurationMs": 6150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "extraordinary that there is a crystal,\nthere is a material that you could heat"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606060,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "up and create negative ions. So the\nreason people wouldn't have tourmaline"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610230,
    "dDurationMs": 6081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lamps is because tourmaline is just\nreally expensive?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 617500,
    "dDurationMs": 1220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "okay so we didn't get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618720,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any ions off of the salt lamp but I\nbrought something along that I think"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623490,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "might give us some ions. This is an ionic\nair purifier. When this product was first"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629850,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "launched it sold a two million units. It\nworks by using high voltage to ionize"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635130,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the air and accelerate those ions to\nproduce the light breeze you can feel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638610,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without any moving parts.\n-Okay I feel a breeze coming out of it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642390,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that should be going into the nozzle?\nwe've got it pointed right at our ion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646860,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Inlet so that's good."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 648260,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We seem to be\nseeing some ions at the moment and we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 650760,
    "dDurationMs": 3473,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have the ionic breeze right up next to\nthe source so."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654233,
    "dDurationMs": 1507,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are negative ions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655740,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these are negative ions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657880,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you want\nnegative ions what you need in your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661200,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "house is not a salt lamp, it's an ionic\nair purifier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665900,
    "dDurationMs": 1390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Before you rush out to buy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667290,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one I should warn you that generating\nthese ions produces an unfortunate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 671760,
    "dDurationMs": 960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by-product:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672720,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ozone. So right now we're\nmeasuring about 17 parts per billion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678300,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually of ozone. So let's put this\nup to the front and see whether or not"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682800,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we see an increase in the amount of\nozone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688500,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's up over 80. So now I think"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691890,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're actually at the level of a smog\nalert."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696140,
    "dDurationMs": 2890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you're saying that this device"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699030,
    "dDurationMs": 6430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is creating air that would be considered\nsmog in a city?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 705460,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I believe so yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709680,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is kind of ridiculous for something that's\nmeant to purify the air. Can you smell"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712980,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ozone? -yeah -whoa"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717100,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Does it trouble you?\nOh, it doesn't bother me. I know it and I"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722010,
    "dDurationMs": 3375,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "want to either leave the lab or turn it\noff."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 725385,
    "dDurationMs": 2475,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What am i smelling for here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727860,
    "dDurationMs": 3030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should... -oh yeah\nthe sweet smell  -oh yeah -that smell a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730890,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "little sweet? \nyeah? \nyeah -I uh..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733380,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A lot of people like\nthat smell but if you smell that it's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736050,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not good. so perhaps we should shut this\noff before we asphyxiate ourselves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740070,
    "dDurationMs": 6300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, generating clean negative\nions is challenging but is it even worth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746370,
    "dDurationMs": 5190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the effort? the research is inconsistent.\nNo significant difference. Evidence for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751560,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "beneficial effects of negative ions on\nmood and performance could not be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 754530,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "demonstrated. Of the studies that report\nsignificant results,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 757530,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many have methodological problems in\nsome participants weren't blinded to the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762480,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "treatment they were receiving. When they\nwere blinded they may still have known"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766470,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when negative ions were present by the\nfaint smell of ozone. Most of the studies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771690,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have very small sample sizes. Plus they\nsurveyed participants on a number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776160,
    "dDurationMs": 3539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of measures increasing the likelihood\nthat at least one would show a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779699,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "significant difference, just due to\nrandom chance. Ion levels were typically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784379,
    "dDurationMs": 3811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "measured at the source and the distance\nto subjects was not tightly controlled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 788190,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nor were the other components of the air\nso there's no guarantee that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792300,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "participants were even receiving the\nexpected levels of ions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796120,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A meta-analysis from 2013 reviewing all the prior human ion studies concluded there was quote \"no"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802680,
    "dDurationMs": 5219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consistent influence of positive or\nnegative air ionization on anxiety mood"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 807899,
    "dDurationMs": 5011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relaxation sleep and personal comfort\nmeasures\" the only link they found was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 812910,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between negative air ionization and\nlower depression scores, though the authors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817350,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "caution future research is needed to\nevaluate the biological plausibility of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821790,
    "dDurationMs": 1190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this association."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822980,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because fundamentally\nthe idea that ions have any biological"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827040,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "effect is implausible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 830100,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Consider that in a\ncubic centimeter of air there are 10 to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833490,
    "dDurationMs": 4769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the 19 air molecules. So even with tens\nof thousands of ions the amount is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838259,
    "dDurationMs": 4351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "insignificant, not even one part per\nbillion we're talking parts per million"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842610,
    "dDurationMs": 4079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "billion. And there's no reason to suspect\nthe extra electrons would do anything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 846689,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anyway. I mean in your daily life\nyou are constantly building up charge on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 851279,
    "dDurationMs": 2521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your skin and discharging it through\nlittle zaps"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 853800,
    "dDurationMs": 3779,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say when you touch a doorknob. What would a few more stray electrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857579,
    "dDurationMs": 3301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "extracellular do? - yeah"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860880,
    "dDurationMs": 4769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Uh, probably not much.\nSo if ions do anything it would likely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865649,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be indirectly say by removing pollutants\nand odors from the air."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869969,
    "dDurationMs": 4441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The ions would cling to the chemicals and then they\nwould say get attracted to surfaces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 874410,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "surfaces and stick to the surface the\nchemicals stay on the surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 877960,
    "dDurationMs": 6410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I think ultimately if you are looking for a way\nto improve your mental and physical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 884370,
    "dDurationMs": 6839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "health that is backed by strong\nscientific evidence, then you should take"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891209,
    "dDurationMs": 4951,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a walk outside. I mean you can walk near\na waterfall or near the ocean if you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896160,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like but the thing that is proven to\nboost your mood is the exercise."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903440,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as an added bonus you're guaranteed\nto get some fresh air."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 919470,
    "dDurationMs": 4930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey this episode was sponsored by\nLastPass. You know I remember the very"
    } ]
  }, {
